u4n|n|An opening in anything made by breaking or parting; as, a gap in a fence; an opening for a passage or entrance; an opening which implies a breach or defect; a vacant space or time; a hiatus; a mountain pass.	a:22ft,44,4;98c,42,1;ynt,35,7;28s5,32,3;h59,30,2;11r2,29,5;7md,21,8;qmh,21,6;19qd,20,2;1593,17,6~7md,21,8;ynt,35,7;qmh,21,6;1593,17,6;11r2,29,5;1vhw,11,5;16r0,8,5;22ft,44,4;zw,16,4;16i4,5,4	v:10te,41,3;asx,12,4;1d2v,6,2~asx,12,4;10te,41,3;1d2v,6,2	n:1td,48,10;10nj,42,4;ug1,38,5;1as8,35,6;e4r,32,5;1v3m,25,2;1hlu,25,3;14n9,24,8;nwq,23,2;1gz1,17,4~1td,48,10;14n9,24,8;1as8,35,6;ug1,38,5;e4r,32,5;29ke,4,5;15ht,11,5;10nj,42,4;1d2v,16,4;1gz1,17,4	N:rr4,31,2;1v0x,22,3~1v0x,22,3;rr4,31,2
